    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i have been paring with the grain and going very slow with light strokes. i even tried sharpening the chisels on a higher grit and using a honing guide to make sure the bevel is perfect. even so, the tips just seem to crumble. could it be the moisture content of the walnut? or maybe something about the way the fibers are laid out in this specific batch?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
