      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Despite your best efforts, the issue may still be related to the walnut's wood structure, which can be particularly challenging to work with. Walnut is known for having a fine, closed grain and a high resin content, which can cause fibers to splinter easily. If you've confirmed the moisture content is within a normal range, it's possible that this specific batch of walnut has an unusually high amount of natural defects, affecting the behavior of the fibers and leading to the crushed fibers.",
